    {
      "id": "sF7UBe95rw7q4Ocowfxzg",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1153.3468896694558,
      "y": -3939.5966834932206,
      "width": 1139.9180908203125,
      "height": 300,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b9T",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1267737676,
      "version": 564,
      "versionNonce": 1058625612,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794869258567,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "=====================================================================================================\nDATABASE (OLTP) VS DATA WAREHOUSE (OLAP)\n=====================================================================================================\nATTRIBUTE        | OLTP DATABASE                          | DATA WAREHOUSE (OLAP)\n-----------------+------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPurpose               | Run the business                           | Analyze the business\nOperations            | Many small reads/writes, lookups        | Few large scans and aggregations\nData                   | Current state, normalized                 | Historical, denormalized (star schema)\nStorage layout       | Row-oriented                                | Column-oriented\nPriorities              | Low latency, concurrency, ACID          | Scan throughput, query flexibility\nFreshness             | Real time                                     | Batch/ETL, minutes to hours\nExamples              | Postgres, MySQL, Oracle, DynamoDB   | Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, ClickHouse",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "=====================================================================================================\nDATABASE (OLTP) VS DATA WAREHOUSE (OLAP)\n=====================================================================================================\nATTRIBUTE        | OLTP DATABASE                          | DATA WAREHOUSE (OLAP)\n-----------------+------------------------------------+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPurpose               | Run the business                           | Analyze the business\nOperations            | Many small reads/writes, lookups        | Few large scans and aggregations\nData                   | Current state, normalized                 | Historical, denormalized (star schema)\nStorage layout       | Row-oriented                                | Column-oriented\nPriorities              | Low latency, concurrency, ACID          | Scan throughput, query flexibility\nFreshness             | Real time                                     | Batch/ETL, minutes to hours\nExamples              | Postgres, MySQL, Oracle, DynamoDB   | Snowflake, BigQuery, Redshift, ClickHouse",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "hasTextLink": false,
      "link": null
    },
